SDL3 3.4.16 local X11 ShowWindow integration fix.

Poll for the existing MapNotify event and verify actual map state rather than
blocking solely on the notification. Preserve the wait when the window remains
unmapped; no timeout or synthetic successful mapping is introduced. Stop polling
on an X display connection error, as the original wait's guard intended.

--- a/src/video/x11/SDL_x11window.c
+++ b/src/video/x11/SDL_x11window.c
@@ -1561,13 +1561,21 @@
 
     if (!X11_IsWindowMapped(_this, window)) {
         X11_XMapRaised(display, data->xwindow);
-        /* Blocking wait for "MapNotify" event.
-         * We use X11_XIfEvent because pXWindowEvent takes a mask rather than a type,
-         * and XCheckTypedWindowEvent doesn't block */
-        if (!(window->flags & SDL_WINDOW_EXTERNAL) && X11_IsDisplayOk(display)) {
-            X11_XIfEvent(display, &event, &isMapNotify, (XPointer)&data->xwindow);
-        }
         X11_XFlush(display);
+        /* Wait for MapNotify or confirmation that the window is mapped. A window
+         * manager can map the window without a matching notification remaining
+         * in our event queue, so an event-only blocking wait can stall forever.
+         * Do not continue while the window is still unmapped.
+         */
+        if (!(window->flags & SDL_WINDOW_EXTERNAL)) {
+            while (X11_IsDisplayOk(display)) {
+                if (X11_XCheckIfEvent(display, &event, &isMapNotify, (XPointer)&data->xwindow) ||
+                    X11_IsWindowMapped(_this, window)) {
+                    break;
+                }
+                SDL_Delay(1);
+            }
+        }
         set_position = data->pending_position ||
                        (!(window->flags & SDL_WINDOW_BORDERLESS) && !window->undefined_x && !window->undefined_y);
     }
